{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated cobbler pipeline (stitch phase) for task #5398 in generation-run44 of the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils utilities based on formal SRD specifications. However, the specific requirements assigned to this task are unclear — the task description says \"Cobbler measure is calling Claude to propose task 0 for generation generation-run44\" which appears to be the measure phase placeholder rather than specific stitch instructions with explicit requirements to implement. I was in the process of determining which requirements were marked in_progress for this task.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils verified via differential testing\n   - Cobbler-scaffold pipeline: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation)\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs Homebrew GNU reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for all cmd/ utilities\n   - Generation branches: code is deleted and regenerated during runs\n   - Requirements tracked in `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` with states (ready, in_progress, etc.)\n   - Package contracts for pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, pkg/hashutil, pkg/sizeparse, pkg/encutil\n   - Task #5397 (previous) implemented cmd/mv with srd057 R2.1-R2.4\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` — Contains requirement states; I tried to diff this to find which requirements were assigned to #5398 but the diff returned empty\n   - All pkg/ source files were provided inline in the prompt (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil) — these are the shared library contracts that cmd/ implementations must follow\n   - The requirement_states section lists many SRDs all with `status: ready`: srd004-ts, srd058-rm, srd060-date, srd061-sleep, srd062-touch, srd063-timeout, srd064-shuf, srd065-factor, srd066-expr, srd067-split, srd068-csplit, srd069-join, srd070-fmt, srd071-numfmt, srd072-od, srd073-printf, srd074-sha224sum, srd075-sha384sum, srd076-b2sum, srd077-cksum, srd078-sum, srd079-base32, srd080-base64, srd081-basenc, srd082-stat, srd083-truncate, srd084-link, srd085-sync, srd089-chmod, srd090-chgrp, srd091-chown, srd092-mkfifo, srd093-mknod, srd094-nice, srd095-nohup, srd096-users, srd097-who, srd098-pinky, srd099-shred, srd100-chroot, srd101-install, srd102-tsort, srd103-pathchk, srd104-test, srd105-stty, srd106-df, srd107-dir, srd108-vdir, srd109-dircolors, srd110-pr, srd111-ptx, srd112-chronic, srd113-pee, srd114-vidir\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `git diff HEAD~1 -- .cobbler/requirements.yaml` returned empty output — this means the requirements changes may not be in that specific file path, or the diff format didn't capture the change. I did not get to investigate further before the summary request.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The core unsolved problem: determining which specific requirements are assigned to task #5398. The task prompt lacks explicit \"Requirements\" and \"Files to Create/Modify\" sections that would normally be present in a stitch task. The git log confirms requirements were marked in_progress for #5398 (commit 38f04c6e) but I couldn't retrieve which ones.\n   - The previous task #5397 was clearly defined as \"[stitch] cmd/mv: srd057 R2.1-R2.4\" suggesting this task should similarly target specific SRD requirements.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The massive stitch task prompt with all project context, constitutions, requirement_states, package_contracts, etc. Key detail: task description says \"Cobbler measure is calling Claude to propose task 0 for generation generation-run44.\"\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — A summary request instructing me to produce an analysis and summary without any tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Determine which specific requirements are assigned to task #5398 (need to read `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` or the latest measure output to find in_progress requirements)\n   - Once requirements are identified: implement the code per the SRD specifications\n   - Verify implementation compiles with `go build` and passes tests with `go test`\n   - Follow all execution constitution rules (copyright headers, SIGPIPE handling, differential testing pattern, no git commands, etc.)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was in the very early investigation phase trying to determine what this task requires. I ran `git log --oneline -5` which showed the commit history confirming task #5398 had requirements marked in_progress. I also ran `git diff HEAD~1 -- .cobbler/requirements.yaml` which returned empty, so I had not yet identified the specific requirements. I was about to investigate further (possibly reading the requirements.yaml file directly or checking the latest measure log/stats files) when the summary request interrupted.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read the `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` file to find which requirements have `status: in_progress` — these are the requirements assigned to task #5398 that need to be implemented. Then read the corresponding SRD specification files (under `docs/specs/software-requirements/`) for those requirements to understand what code to write. The most recent work was investigating the commit \"Mark requirements in_progress for #5398\" to find the assignment. The git diff was empty, so the next step is to directly read the requirements file.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-pr